I come back to the flat from my shift at the café.
Bruno is already waiting for me at the door.
He is very happy, wags his tail and runs into the living room.
It is a warm, bright afternoon.
The late spring is really beautiful.
That is the perfect weather for a long walk.
I take Bruno's lead from the hook on the wall.
He jumps up immediately.
"Come here, Bruno!" I call.
He quickly runs to me.
I clip the lead to his collar.
Sabine says I must always keep him on the lead outside.
A dog is not allowed to run without a lead in the city.
That is important for his safety.
I open the front door.
Then I happily take him outside with me.
We have a nice, long walk ahead of us.
